claim.claim-text:
a semiconductor substrate (160);
a conductive region (20) disposed in or on the semiconductor substrate (160); and
an electrode (42) comprising a plurality of finger lines (42a) connected to the conductive region (20), and formed to extend in a first direction while being parallel, and 6 or more bus bar lines (42b) formed to extend in a second direction crossing the first direction, wherein each of the bus bar lines (42b) has a width of 35 to 350µm at at least a portion thereof.

the edge distance is 2.37 to 9.78mm when the width of the plurality of leads is equal to or greater than 250µm, but less than 300µm;
the edge distance is 3.99 to 12.94mm when the width of the plurality of leads is equal to or greater than 300µm, but less than 350µm;
the edge distance is 5.06 to 15.98mm when the width of the plurality of leads is equal to or greater than 350µm, but less than 400µm;
the edge distance is 5.69 to 18.96mm when the width of the plurality of leads is equal to or greater than 400µm, but less than 450µm; and
the edge distance is 5.94 to 21.94mm when the width of the plurality of leads is equal to or greater than 450µm, but less than 500µm.
